51	{"parentUuid":"d003ceb8-f425-40e9-82dc-07ac63faccf9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"597c53bc-3bad-40ea-b0af-d096b711d46e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016HBfLu3VvTmafBEavy2oyf","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"number\":153,\"title\":\"claudinite-dashboard adoption: the setup steps only a human can do\",\"body\":\"Adopting `claudinite-dashboard` (#152) brings three steps no Action can perform. Each is quoted from the pack\\u0026#39;s own `adoptionHandover`, with what breaks while it is off and what closes it.\\n\\n- [ ] **Enable GitHub Pages on this repo with source \\u0026#34;GitHub Actions\\u0026#34;** — [Settings → Pages](https://github.com/missingbulb/ClaudiniteCanary/settings/pages).\\n  - while off: the deploy job fails on every run; the build still succeeds, so nothing else is affected\\n  - done when: the Pages URL serves the dashboard, and the Claudinite dashboard workflow is green\\n  - *note:* missingbulb/Claudinite#1158 records this as already done ahead of the adoption. The first `Claudinite dashboard` run after #153 merges is what confirms it — if that run is green, tick this and move on.\\n\\n- [ ] **Add the Actions secret `FLEET_GITHUB_TOKEN`** — [Settings → Secrets → Actions](https://github.com/missingbulb/ClaudiniteCanary/settings/secrets/actions). A fine-grained PAT on this account covering **all** repositories, granted Metadata read, Contents read, Issues read, Pull requests read.\\n  - while off: the daily `fleet-digest` task parks asking for the secret, so no brief is written and the dashboard\\u0026#39;s brief series has a hole for every day it is missing; the page itself still builds\\n  - done when: the secret exists and the next `fleet-digest` run writes a brief\\n  - *this one has teeth here:* the pack has no config gate for the digest task, so a repo that adopts it for the page alone gets the task too. Until the secret exists, expect a parked work item every day.\\n\\n- [ ] **Decide how this dashboard authenticates its viewers** — leave it on the pasted-token box (nothing to do), or give it a Sign in button: register a GitHub App with read-only Contents, Issues and Actions, install it on the account holding these repos, deploy the pack\\u0026#39;s `oauth-exchange` example, and set `clientId` and `exchangeUrl` on this pack\\u0026#39;s declaration. See \\u0026#34;Who has to register the app\\u0026#34; in the pack README — one App serves every deployment you own, and none can be inherited from another owner.\\n  - while off: nothing fails, but a viewer who has not pasted a token reads GitHub anonymously at 60 requests/hour per IP — which one fleet sweep exceeds, so the page serves cached data or empty rows until the hour rolls\\n  - done when: a signed-in viewer sees the rate pill read \\u0026#34;…/5000 · user\\u0026#34;, **or** this repo has recorded that the token box is this deployment\\u0026#39;s answer\\n\\nCloses nothing on its own — this issue closes when all three boxes are ticked.\",\"state\":\"open\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/missingbulb/ClaudiniteCanary/issues/153\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"missingbulb\",\"id\":73882448,\"profile_url\":\"https://github.com/missingbulb\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73882448?v=4\"},\"author_association\":\"OWNER\",\"assignees\":[],\"comments\":1,\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:10:39Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:11:01Z\",\"has_parent\":false,\"has_children\":false,\"closed_by_pull_requests\":{\"total_count\":0,\"references\":[]}}"}]}]},"uuid":"7b890f49-9f2e-44a6-a87a-20375a93bb57","timestamp":"2026-08-22T04:47:56.050Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"number\":153,\"title\":\"claudinite-dashboard adoption: the setup steps only a human can do\",\"body\":\"Adopting `claudinite-dashboard` (#152) brings three steps no Action can perform. Each is quoted from the pack\\u0026#39;s own `adoptionHandover`, with what breaks while it is off and what closes it.\\n\\n- [ ] **Enable GitHub Pages on this repo with source \\u0026#34;GitHub Actions\\u0026#34;** — [Settings → Pages](https://github.com/missingbulb/ClaudiniteCanary/settings/pages).\\n  - while off: the deploy job fails on every run; the build still succeeds, so nothing else is affected\\n  - done when: the Pages URL serves the dashboard, and the Claudinite dashboard workflow is green\\n  - *note:* missingbulb/Claudinite#1158 records this as already done ahead of the adoption. The first `Claudinite dashboard` run after #153 merges is what confirms it — if that run is green, tick this and move on.\\n\\n- [ ] **Add the Actions secret `FLEET_GITHUB_TOKEN`** — [Settings → Secrets → Actions](https://github.com/missingbulb/ClaudiniteCanary/settings/secrets/actions). A fine-grained PAT on this account covering **all** repositories, granted Metadata read, Contents read, Issues read, Pull requests read.\\n  - while off: the daily `fleet-digest` task parks asking for the secret, so no brief is written and the dashboard\\u0026#39;s brief series has a hole for every day it is missing; the page itself still builds\\n  - done when: the secret exists and the next `fleet-digest` run writes a brief\\n  - *this one has teeth here:* the pack has no config gate for the digest task, so a repo that adopts it for the page alone gets the task too. Until the secret exists, expect a parked work item every day.\\n\\n- [ ] **Decide how this dashboard authenticates its viewers** — leave it on the pasted-token box (nothing to do), or give it a Sign in button: register a GitHub App with read-only Contents, Issues and Actions, install it on the account holding these repos, deploy the pack\\u0026#39;s `oauth-exchange` example, and set `clientId` and `exchangeUrl` on this pack\\u0026#39;s declaration. See \\u0026#34;Who has to register the app\\u0026#34; in the pack 